CORE
main.c
--custom-bitvector-analysis
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^file main\.c line 6 function main, set: TRUE$
^file main\.c line 7 function main, set, via p: TRUE$
^file main\.c line 9 function main, cleared: FALSE$
^file main\.c line 10 function main, never set: TRUE$
^SUMMARY: 3 pass, 1 fail, 0 unknown$
--
--
The pointer arguments of __CPROVER_get_must and __CPROVER_get_may are cast to
void *, which the analysis used not to see through, so that every query on &x
was false.  goto-instrument does not write a goto binary for this option, and
chain.sh then runs cbmc on the original program: cbmc ignores the queries
(with a warning), and the assertions using them fail.
